### Page 1 of 2

```text
RESOLUTION NO. ________

ENTITLED:
"A RESOLUTION SUPPORTING THE CITY OF CHEYENNE’S
APPLICATION FOR TRANSPORTATION ALTERNATIVES PROGRAM
(TAP) FUNDING, FOR IMPLEMENTATION OF THE WAYFINDING
PLAN."

WHEREAS, the Transportation Alternatives Program (TAP) funds may be used for projects or
activities that are related to surface transportation and described in the definition of “Transportation
Alternatives.” [23 USC 101(a)(29)]; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne’s FY `14 application involves implementing the May, 2010
Cheyenne Wayfinding Plan; and

WHEREAS, the Cheyenne Wayfinding Plan was approved by the Cheyenne Governing Body in
June, 2010; and

WHEREAS, total build-out of this project is estimated to cost $520,000 and the City of
Cheyenne is asking for a grant of $400,000.  Visit Cheyenne and the Downtown Development
Association will each contribute $15,000 to the project, and a Wyoming Tourism grant will provide
$20,000.  The City 5th Penny Sales Tax funds (`07-`10, `11-`14) will provide the balance of $70,000;
and

WHEREAS, the Cheyenne Wayfinding Plan will standardize much of the signage in Cheyenne
and help locals and visitors find their way throughout our community; and

WHEREAS,  Cheyenne Metropolitan Planning Organization (MPO) prepared the Cheyenne
Wayfinding Plan with public input in coordination with the City of Cheyenne, Laramie County, Visit
Cheyenne, and the Wyoming Department of Transportation; and

WHEREAS,  the proposed project is listed in the Federal Fiscal Year `14 - `17 MPO
Transportation Improvement Program (TIP) approved by the Policy, Technical and Citizens’ Advisory
Committees and therefore submitted to the Wyoming Department of Transportation for inclusion in the
Wyoming State Transportation Improvement Plan (STIP); and

WHEREAS, plans and cost estimates for the proposed project have been conducted, identified
and reviewed by the City of Cheyenne; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne supports this proposed project and pledges the local cash
match; and

WHEREAS, the City of Cheyenne is willing and able to follow all federal, state, and local
requirements necessary to complete the proposed project; and

WHEREAS, the proposed project could be ready for implementation within Federal FY `14.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF
CHEYENNE, WYOMING:

That the City of Cheyenne agrees with and supports the application for Transportation Alternatives
Program funding for the implementation of the Cheyenne Wayfinding Plan, as presented to the
Wyoming Department of Transportation as an eligible activity for Transportation Alternatives Program
funding.  Further, the Mayor is authorized to sign the grant agreement if grant funds are awarded.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED THIS _________ DAY OF JULY, 2013.

Richard L. Kaysen, Mayor

(Seal)

ATTEST:

Carol Inlekofer, City Clerk

TAP Res 13 WayFinding.docx
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
Transportation Alternatives Program (TAP)  Grant  2013-2014
Wayfinding Plan Implementation

Our TAP grant project is the implementation of the Cheyenne Wayfinding Plan.  The proposed
project will serve as an integral part of Cheyenne’s directional signage system, making
navigating Cheyenne easier for visitors.  This project will serve to identifying important sites,
features and attractions.

The adopted Cheyenne Wayfinding Plan is ready to go to bid. The project could begin to be
implemented in the fall of  2013.   The implementation of the Cheyenne Wayfinding Plan, will
provide an important connective transportation element for the Cheyenne community.  There
will be fewer lost visitors!

The City is requesting $400,000 from the Transportation Alternatives Program (TAP) grant for
the $520,000  Cheyenne Wayfinding Plan implementation.  The $120,000 balance will come
from the 5th Penny Sales Tax @ $70,000, a Wyoming Department of Tourism grant (requested
by Visit Cheyenne) @ $20,000 and $15,000 each from Visit Cheyenne and the Downtown
Development Association.

TAP13 Backup.doc
```
